---
import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// The CV link only appears once public/cv.pdf exists.
const hasCV = existsSync('./public/cv.pdf');
---
<Base title="Ribhu Hooja">
  <header class="intro">
    <img class="photo" src="/photo.jpg" alt="Photo of Ribhu Hooja" width="450" height="600" />
    <div>
      <h1>Ribhu Hooja</h1>
      <p>
        I am a fourth-year undergraduate math major at Dartmouth College. My research interests are in
        Floer homology, low-dimensional topology, and spectral geometry. I'm drawn to the idea of using
        analytic invariants to study the topology and geometry of a space.
      </p>
      <p class="links">
        <a href="mailto:ribhu.hooja.27@dartmouth.edu">ribhu.hooja.27@dartmouth.edu</a><br />
        {hasCV && <><a href="/cv.pdf">CV</a> · </>}
        <a href="https://github.com/ribhuhooja">GitHub</a> ·
        <a href="https://ribhuhooja.xyz">Notes</a>
        <!-- TODO: LinkedIn -->
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <h2>Research</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/papers/shur-writeup-provisional.pdf">τ and ϵ invariants of generalized Mazur patterns</a>
      (in progress)<br />
      with Sean Kim, Filip Rupchin, Shreya Sinha, and Allison Tsypin
    </li>
    <li>
      <em>Spectral Geometries in Three Dimensions</em>, senior thesis (expository), advised by Craig Sutton.
      <span class="todo">TODO: PDF</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Writing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The Lefschetz fixed-point theorem: notes for the graduate seminar on the Weil conjectures, January 2026. <span class="todo">TODO: PDF</span></li>
    <li>Tangents, cotangents, derivations and differentials: expository worksheet with solutions, Math 121. <span class="todo">TODO: PDFs</span></li>
    <li>Milnor's exotic 7-spheres: term paper, in progress. <span class="todo">TODO: add when done</span></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Talks</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><em>Satellite operations and bordered Heegaard Floer homology</em>. Dartmouth Topology Seminar, September 24, 2026.</li>
    <li><em>Sunada's method: using group theory to construct isospectral drums</em>. HRUMC, April 25, 2026.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Code</h2>
  <p class="todo">TODO: SHUR immersed-curves computation code (GitHub link).</p>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; align-items: flex-start; }
  .photo { width: 160px; height: auto; border-radius: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .intro h1 { margin-top: 0; }
  .links { line-height: 1.8; }
  .todo { color: #b00; font-size: 0.9em; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  li { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .intro { flex-direction: column; }
  }
</style>
